[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station in upland Scotland. Mainly natural regime with a small headwater diversion into the Shin catchment. GENERAL: Velocity area station about 40m wide with relatively stable cobble control at the end of the measuring reach. STATION HYDROMETRY: Ratings derived from current meter gaugings up to 161 cumecs (about QMED), simple extrapolation beyond. Peak flow rating revised in 2016 and used for whole period of record. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8). FLOW REGIME: Mainly natural regime. Small headwater diversion into the Shin catchment (HEP). Major storage in Loch Brora (no control).
CATCHMENT,Mountainous headwaters, often snowy in winter. Predominantly Moinian metamorphic rocks with granitic intrusions. Bedrock predominantly impermeable with extensive superficial deposits. Rough pasture and moorland, some forest, with arable land d/s. No significant catchment changes known.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Rating based on gaugings up to 2.1m (measured flow of 161 cumecs) followed by simple extrapolation.
